        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L1-L3",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e74ed2674c401b2d30d0536ab77d42407094527dcbccf0a565c036467504c9f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cd3588bf205d40ad93507bf98bce81ff",
      "statement": "GasBee nRF powers the HX711 from the XIAO's 3V3 rail (DOUT=P0.28/D2, PD_SCK=P0.29/D3), limits LiPo charge current to approximately 100mA by holding HICHG (P0.13) permanently low via a gpio-hog, and has not yet measured the actual charge current on hardware.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L24-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ae8fb449ff6e4994aa1f038059ab863e161b8b9cbabd64420d3b22cace9beb76:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L9-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:74a67caacddf944fa7bd0e4acbf861969fd40f686a7e90a7175714cb6f674383:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_10120552f5e3438eb123090b5ee06b60",
      "statement": "GasBee nRF runs a measurement cycle every CONFIG_GASBEE_MEASURE_INTERVAL_S (default 300s, 60s in test mode): wake HX711 and discard 4 conversions, average 5 samples, power down the HX711, read battery/charge status, then send a 10-packet advertising burst spaced 1s apart followed by radio silence until the next cycle.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L53-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:747c190d99c197276faf34c0f91106afd1b8b7fffe5021937d1e43c91774e60c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_273730d19b954ca78f0fbaa7238d66e8",
      "statement": "GasBee nRF enters USB configuration mode within 2 seconds of detecting VBUS (polled via nrf_power_usbregstatus_vbusdet_get): it advertises every second and is connectable, measures every 5s, sets advertising flag bit 3, and only accepts writes to calibration characteristics 0x2B11-0x2B13 in this mode (ATT 'Write Not Permitted' otherwise); unplugging USB disconnects any client and returns it to the 5-minute battery cadence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L63-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:75dc28b660e290b71ba19eeba3f73e4002c6fe58c02f623d70dece8b8bdafcd3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9c0d72d5178e4286aaffadf26840ceec",
      "statement": "GasBee nRF's BLE advertising format v1 encodes format version, gross (untared) weight in 10g units, battery voltage in mV, a per-cycle sequence counter shared by all 10 burst packets, and a status flag byte (HX711 ok, charging, calibrated, configuration mode); tare, net gas weight, fill percentage, and battery percentage are computed by the Sensorboard, not the node.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L75-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8535ece88035d83cd71ce442bbd6df360b5761be90787968090d92fa033e4c40:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0735f611cbd94f7a8557baef7ae9acf8",
      "statement": "GasBee nRF's GATT service (compatible superset of the ESP32-C3 GATT layout plus a 0x2B04 battery-voltage characteristic and 0x2B11-0x2B13 calibration characteristics) is not used by the Sensorboard; it remains connectable for third-party clients, and while a GATT client is connected the node suspends its advertising bursts, so the Sensorboard receives no updates until disconnect.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L95-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a291f625d1875866f171b6cdd6211daa4ec8070a87f21ef050a34e133002ed6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0feeea18412a457481206f3567b443be",
      "statement": "GasBee nRF calibration (offset, scale) is stored per device in NVS and survives reset/firmware updates; without stored values it falls back to compile-time defaults in gasbee_config.h and reports flag bit 2 = 0 (not calibrated), and a write to the tare characteristic 0x2B10 latches the next measured gross weight as the new tare, unlike the ESP32-C3 GasBee where tare only zeroed the offset without a true zero-point measurement.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L207-L239",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cfa060de0d4b9dde190051f346a13231575b6998b4158b692530cc9a463a2a9c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b609bd5f1261401d920fac259f8e93bb",
      "statement": "The legacy ESP32-C3 GasBee averages 5 HX711 samples every 5 seconds on a single channel (GPIO4 DOUT / GPIO5 SCK), advertises at a fixed 500ms interval, and exposes a GATT-only data path (0x2B01 weight, 0x2B02 fill%, 0x2B03 net gas, 0x2B10 tare) with no battery-voltage characteristic and no advertising-encoded sensor data.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee/main/ble_gas.c#L99-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28e051c041e22b02fceefb13a1c37b02a9dd884dc03a39a790523868b6a52844:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee/main/gasbee_config.h#L14-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1323ae1246f5ac3a97f96c3a6d1aa0081651f0c4e2a6005434710a5c08cb8b3b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9159e7fd79664837ba35fac338774645",
      "statement": "RuuviTag Gas is a hardware fork of RuuviTag Rev.B8 intended to eventually replace the ESP32-C3 GasBee with an nRF52832-based gas-bottle beacon, but as of the current state it is hardware-fork-in-progress (Phase 2 schematic done, PCB layout not started) and firmware work has not begun, making it a distinct future project rather than an alternative to the shipping GasBee nRF.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://hardware/schematics/ruuvitag_gas/README.md#L1-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5ca4b010e3758ab5e7a1586c1475ef8e9e60271dae0617412fe251d61fd8e50:"
        },
        {
