          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:80afc5e1c553b1f6644884b3c27987641e9faa03a802e9f426862d72e487acb8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5c52592703c446b1a0003a91b0683b38",
      "statement": "RuuviTag Gas's planned design removes the Rev.B8 pressure/accelerometer/temperature sensors (DPS310, LIS2DH12, TMP117) and their SPI bus, keeps SHTC3 for temperature/humidity, and adds an HX711 load-cell ADC gated by a dedicated high-side P-MOSFET load switch (HX711_EN on P0.03) so the HX711 and bridge draw near-zero current when idle, a design chosen specifically because the GasBee nRF's always-on 3V3-fed HX711 approach is unacceptable against RuuviTag's CR2477 coin-cell budget.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://hardware/schematics/ruuvitag_gas/PHASE2_HX711.md#L59-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac59e78639bbc16a5a8214de848058addc3b46e66d0c30c1f5a16d0aaa8e6fd1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://hardware/schematics/ruuvitag_gas/README.md#L12-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5cebe78b1ea2bf0f8d34410ac5d5c9716be593932bd846dae7d9cce9277b316f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4588755f0b924ca8b908cb6a726f7668",
      "statement": "Stock RuuviTag tags broadcasting Ruuvi Data Format 5 (RAWv2) serve as an indoor/outdoor climate fallback: the Sensorboard's ruuvi_ble_scanner decodes them as a passive-scan handler on the shared ble_manager radio, routes two slots (indoor/outdoor) by a runtime-configurable MAC filter persisted in NVS, extracts temp/humidity/pressure/battery fields, and always yields precedence to a wired BME680/BME280 sensor for the same location.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/memory-bank/systemPatterns.md#L104-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd7d9af0bb62bb287742639af448a6d1712407736c4b5db7cf60b74fc7b09328:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_56c334d05e2f40e3be4d421545a96a1c",
      "statement": "All BLE sensor nodes documented here (GasBee ESP32-C3, GasBee nRF, planned RuuviTag Gas, stock Ruuvi DF5) share a single Sensorboard NimBLE radio operating in passive-scan mode; any transient connection to a node (legacy GasBee GATT client, or GasBee nRF calibration/third-party client) blocks that node's advertising bursts and the Sensorboard sees no fresh data from it until the connection ends.",
      "evidence": [
